# Ironhide — ASUS laptop: RTX 4060 Max-Q (dGPU) + AMD Phoenix1 iGPU.
#
# The iGPU is primary for battery; run apps on the dGPU with: prime-run <app>
#
# Userspace only. The kernel MODULE and matching headers are derived at
# bootstrap time by resolve_kernel_packages, which now reads the PCI vendor IDs
# rather than guessing from the class — so a laptop without an NVIDIA card gets
# no NVIDIA modules even though it is also class=laptop.

# --- NVIDIA dGPU (userspace) ---
nvidia-utils
libva-nvidia-driver
nvidia-prime

# --- AMD iGPU ---
vulkan-radeon

# --- 32-bit halves, for Steam/Proton through prime-run ---
lib32-nvidia-utils
lib32-vulkan-radeon
